1
00:01:30,007 --> 00:01:51,767
I've had way too much to drink.

2
00:01:52,447 --> 00:01:52,927
Idiot.

3
00:01:53,147 --> 00:01:55,587
You're not supposed to kill any of the hostages, Chess.

4
00:01:55,927 --> 00:01:57,007
Oh, crap.

5
00:01:57,427 --> 00:01:58,047
Hey, human.

6
00:01:58,047 --> 00:01:59,847
You can't die without my permission.

7
00:02:00,007 --> 00:02:00,527
Okay?

8
00:02:01,887 --> 00:02:03,707
I'm so sorry, Lord Crowley.

9
00:02:03,847 --> 00:02:05,047
I got carried away.

10
00:02:05,967 --> 00:02:07,227
Don't worry about it.

11
00:02:07,547 --> 00:02:09,627
We've got plenty more where he came from.

12
00:02:10,087 --> 00:02:10,767
Hear that, Horn?

13
00:02:11,287 --> 00:02:13,547
You should have some, too, while he's still warm.

14
00:02:14,207 --> 00:02:16,747
When are you going to learn to exhibit a little self-control?

15
00:02:17,127 --> 00:02:18,667
You're a noble, not a savage.

16
00:02:19,347 --> 00:02:19,827
Jeez.

17
00:02:20,207 --> 00:02:21,787
Keep acting all uptight like that

18
00:02:21,787 --> 00:02:23,427
and you'll miss out on all the good stuff.

19
00:02:23,867 --> 00:02:25,467
Wouldn't you agree with me, Lord Crowley?

20
00:02:25,647 --> 00:02:28,427
It wouldn't hurt for you to take life more seriously.

21
00:02:28,727 --> 00:02:28,967
What?

22
00:02:28,967 --> 00:02:30,667
Come on.

23
00:02:31,547 --> 00:02:33,487
We need to discuss today's attacks.

24
00:02:33,867 --> 00:02:36,087
It seems the humans finally found their backbones.

25
00:02:37,107 --> 00:02:39,507
This Nagoya invasion of theirs was an act of war

26
00:02:39,507 --> 00:02:40,687
and we must strike back.

27
00:02:41,627 --> 00:02:42,027
Hmm.

28
00:02:42,687 --> 00:02:44,007
You're right about that.

29
00:02:44,007 --> 00:03:00,587
Hey, Chess.

30
00:03:00,587 --> 00:03:02,747
Come here for a second, will you?

31
00:03:03,927 --> 00:03:04,327
Huh?

32
00:03:05,187 --> 00:03:06,267
Yeah, okay.

33
00:03:06,267 --> 00:03:18,207
Uh, what did you do that for?

34
00:03:18,887 --> 00:03:22,267
Well, I just wanted to see which weapon was stronger.

35
00:03:22,647 --> 00:03:24,767
A human's blade or that of a vampire.

36
00:03:24,767 --> 00:03:29,787
But, Lord Crowley, whichever weapon you hold is bound to be the strongest one, isn't it?

37
00:03:30,227 --> 00:03:32,727
True, but that's not what I'm interested in.

38
00:03:33,047 --> 00:03:34,407
Could you elaborate, my lord?

39
00:03:35,047 --> 00:03:35,427
Hmm.

40
00:03:35,427 --> 00:03:39,927
I'm afraid the humans are gaining too much power too quickly.

41
00:03:40,307 --> 00:03:42,727
That's how they managed to take down so many nobles.

42
00:03:42,727 --> 00:03:50,987
Just look at this weapon.

43
00:03:51,167 --> 00:03:53,367
It's cursed, so it could kill any one of us.

44
00:03:54,187 --> 00:03:57,487
However, this isn't the sort of thing they'd figure out on their own.

45
00:03:57,487 --> 00:03:59,467
Someone must be leaking them information.

46
00:04:00,287 --> 00:04:04,467
My lord, are you suggesting there might be a traitor among us working with the humans?

47
00:04:05,107 --> 00:04:07,447
Yes, and a high-ranking one at that.

48
00:04:11,887 --> 00:04:12,367
See?

49
00:04:12,787 --> 00:04:15,267
Thanks to this curse, this wound isn't healing at all.

50
00:04:15,667 --> 00:04:17,567
You girls need to be careful out there, okay?

51
00:04:18,127 --> 00:04:19,727
I'll get you a bandage right away.

52
00:04:20,067 --> 00:04:21,727
You can drink from it if you like.

53
00:04:21,807 --> 00:04:22,007
Huh?

54
00:04:22,327 --> 00:04:22,507
Ah!

55
00:04:23,047 --> 00:04:25,387
But, Lord Crowley, I'm not worthy.

56
00:04:25,387 --> 00:04:27,307
In that case, can I have a drink?

57
00:04:27,487 --> 00:04:30,467
You already drained to that human, now you're just being greedy.

58
00:04:30,947 --> 00:04:32,587
I'll accept your gracious offer.

59
00:04:33,127 --> 00:04:34,047
No fair!

60
00:04:34,147 --> 00:04:35,667
Why does she get to taste it?

61
00:04:48,007 --> 00:04:49,367
Is there something wrong?

62
00:04:49,927 --> 00:04:50,287
Hmm.

63
00:04:50,807 --> 00:04:55,287
I was just wondering who the puppet master for this ambitious human operation might be.

64
00:04:55,287 --> 00:04:56,327
Let's think.

65
00:04:56,327 --> 00:05:00,287
Was it Queen Krul-Tepish or perhaps Ferret Bathory's doing?

66
00:05:01,327 --> 00:05:02,327
Or maybe even...

67
00:05:03,467 --> 00:05:04,167
Maybe who?

68
00:05:06,107 --> 00:05:07,187
Never mind.

69
00:05:07,447 --> 00:05:10,867
It can't be possible that a human's responsible for pulling the strings.

70
00:05:10,867 --> 00:05:35,747
So, how long do we have to wait around here exactly?

71
00:05:35,747 --> 00:05:38,547
The other squad should be joining us by 2.20.

72
00:05:38,727 --> 00:05:40,147
Okay, but what if they don't show?

73
00:05:41,147 --> 00:05:42,967
Then we have to assume that they're dead.

74
00:05:43,287 --> 00:05:44,107
What's the time?

75
00:05:47,527 --> 00:05:48,747
Already 2.13.

76
00:05:48,747 --> 00:06:02,787
Is the lieutenant colonel here?

77
00:06:03,207 --> 00:06:04,427
No, not yet.

78
00:06:04,687 --> 00:06:05,127
I see.

79
00:06:05,987 --> 00:06:07,347
Stand by for the time being.

80
00:06:07,567 --> 00:06:08,087
Yes, ma'am.

81
00:06:08,087 --> 00:06:10,007
Hey, Shinua.

82
00:06:10,007 --> 00:06:10,387
Hmm?

83
00:06:10,387 --> 00:06:10,427
Hmm?

84
00:06:10,427 --> 00:06:14,527
Weren't there 15 soldiers on that squad when we set out earlier?

85
00:06:14,787 --> 00:06:15,467
There were.

86
00:06:21,467 --> 00:06:22,947
They lost so many.

87
00:06:22,947 --> 00:06:31,207
Aihara, did your team complete their mission?

88
00:06:31,747 --> 00:06:33,427
We wouldn't be here if we hadn't.

89
00:06:36,167 --> 00:06:38,447
You didn't lose any members of your squad.

90
00:06:39,107 --> 00:06:39,907
I know.

91
00:06:40,027 --> 00:06:40,687
I'm incredible.

92
00:06:41,087 --> 00:06:41,767
Shut up.

93
00:06:42,547 --> 00:06:43,447
Hey, Shinua.

94
00:06:43,707 --> 00:06:45,427
Tell her what a great leader I am.

95
00:06:45,427 --> 00:06:45,987
What?

96
00:06:46,387 --> 00:06:48,627
Come on, why are you dragging me into this?

97
00:06:50,607 --> 00:06:52,427
Um, I mean...

98
00:06:52,967 --> 00:06:58,227
Hey, I'm glad you made it back alive.

99
00:06:58,807 --> 00:07:00,267
We've got this area locked down.

100
00:07:00,587 --> 00:07:01,627
You guys get some rest.

101
00:07:02,327 --> 00:07:03,687
This is one of the newbies?

102
00:07:03,927 --> 00:07:04,447
That's right.

103
00:07:04,907 --> 00:07:06,267
Now, what was his name again?

104
00:07:07,647 --> 00:07:09,487
Don't tell me you've forgotten already!

105
00:07:10,147 --> 00:07:12,987
And after giving me so much crap about not remembering our target.

106
00:07:13,307 --> 00:07:14,427
Just joking around.

107
00:07:14,427 --> 00:07:16,347
He's Yuichiro, Hyakuya.

108
00:07:17,047 --> 00:07:17,767
I see.

109
00:07:18,787 --> 00:07:19,767
Thanks, Hyakuya.

110
00:07:20,067 --> 00:07:23,447
We'll take you up on your offer and use this time to recover some of our strength.

111
00:07:23,947 --> 00:07:25,167
Please keep your eyes open.

112
00:07:25,747 --> 00:07:26,167
Sure.

113
00:07:26,407 --> 00:07:27,327
We've got your backs.

114
00:07:27,327 --> 00:07:45,047
I guess this war really does have casualties.

115
00:07:45,047 --> 00:07:48,327
That's right.

116
00:07:48,807 --> 00:07:49,847
Many comrades will die.

117
00:07:50,387 --> 00:07:51,627
But that's a soldier's life.

118
00:07:52,667 --> 00:07:53,127
Trust me.

119
00:07:53,427 --> 00:07:54,547
I know all about it.

120
00:07:54,967 --> 00:07:56,927
That's why we have to make each day count.

121
00:07:57,427 --> 00:07:59,247
If our lives are short, we'll live them together.

122
00:07:59,247 --> 00:08:06,467
What are you guys doing standing around out here like lost puppies?

123
00:08:07,467 --> 00:08:09,227
So tell me, did you complete your mission?

124
00:08:09,887 --> 00:08:11,167
Yeah, we killed our guy.

125
00:08:11,307 --> 00:08:12,747
And what about your squad?

126
00:08:13,207 --> 00:08:14,147
Piece of cake.

127
00:08:14,427 --> 00:08:15,247
Yeah, right.

128
00:08:15,247 --> 00:08:17,387
Narumi.

129
00:08:18,007 --> 00:08:18,667
Yes, sir.

130
00:08:19,127 --> 00:08:20,727
So how did our noobs fare today?

131
00:08:21,047 --> 00:08:22,347
Did they drag you down too much?

132
00:08:23,667 --> 00:08:23,987
Huh.

133
00:08:25,667 --> 00:08:27,487
They managed to survive at least.

134
00:08:28,927 --> 00:08:31,707
Actually, they did an outstanding job.

135
00:08:32,267 --> 00:08:33,927
Really, each of them impressed me.

136
00:08:34,507 --> 00:08:34,807
Huh.

137
00:08:35,387 --> 00:08:36,147
What's that?

138
00:08:36,327 --> 00:08:37,307
Say it again louder.

139
00:08:37,527 --> 00:08:38,847
Don't get full of yourself.

140
00:08:38,847 --> 00:08:40,307
That hurt.

141
00:08:50,067 --> 00:08:52,667
AiHara, you lost eight of your men?

142
00:08:53,187 --> 00:08:55,147
Um, they were killed, sir.

143
00:08:56,007 --> 00:08:56,807
I apologize.

144
00:08:57,647 --> 00:08:58,387
Lieutenant Colonel.

145
00:08:59,747 --> 00:09:01,347
I failed my squad.

146
00:09:01,987 --> 00:09:03,087
I knew there'd be losses.

147
00:09:03,587 --> 00:09:06,067
Our comrades' deaths are on my hands, not yours.

148
00:09:06,187 --> 00:09:06,767
No, sir.

149
00:09:06,767 --> 00:09:08,327
I should have been a better leader.

150
00:09:08,847 --> 00:09:09,807
Listen to me.

151
00:09:10,387 --> 00:09:12,067
You saved six of your men.

152
00:09:16,167 --> 00:09:18,047
Narumi, any word from the others?

153
00:09:18,727 --> 00:09:19,367
Nothing, sir.

154
00:09:20,087 --> 00:09:20,687
All right, then.

155
00:09:21,207 --> 00:09:23,107
There's no time to stand around and wait.

156
00:09:23,447 --> 00:09:25,807
We'll have to go ahead and start our next mission without them.

157
00:09:26,107 --> 00:09:27,367
What are we gonna do now?

158
00:09:29,407 --> 00:09:32,107
The soldiers assigned to kill the three nobles in City Hall

159
00:09:32,107 --> 00:09:33,767
found themselves completely overwhelmed.

160
00:09:34,487 --> 00:09:37,007
The vampires are holding 25 of them hostage.

161
00:09:37,007 --> 00:09:38,967
Oh, no.

162
00:09:41,647 --> 00:09:44,327
We're definitely gonna need those men for future missions.

163
00:09:44,907 --> 00:09:49,287
Our new objective is to kill the three nobles and rescue our comrades.

164
00:09:49,287 --> 00:09:54,647
Lieutenant Colonel, please let me go on this mission, too.

165
00:09:54,867 --> 00:09:56,347
I would really like to be of assistance.

166
00:09:56,627 --> 00:09:57,347
Not a chance.

167
00:09:57,907 --> 00:10:00,187
I've got no room for someone who cries on the battlefield.

168
00:10:00,187 --> 00:10:03,827
I'm kidding, okay?

169
00:10:03,827 --> 00:10:07,447
Once we're done at City Hall, we'll rendezvous at the airport.

170
00:10:08,147 --> 00:10:11,887
I need you to stay here and relay that information to the other squads that show up.

171
00:10:12,327 --> 00:10:13,307
I'm counting on you.

172
00:10:14,107 --> 00:10:15,007
Yes, sir!

173
00:10:17,247 --> 00:10:17,767
Right.

174
00:10:18,047 --> 00:10:19,247
Let's get moving, kids.

175
00:10:19,767 --> 00:10:20,527
Yes, sir!

176
00:10:20,527 --> 00:10:39,367
Got a second?

177
00:10:39,767 --> 00:10:40,467
Let me guess.

178
00:10:40,707 --> 00:10:43,347
You want to talk me out of this plan because it's likely a trap?

179
00:10:43,347 --> 00:10:45,927
No, I get that we don't have a choice.

180
00:10:46,687 --> 00:10:48,907
We need those squads to win this war.

181
00:10:49,107 --> 00:10:51,527
It's not like there are many humans left to take their places.

182
00:10:52,107 --> 00:10:53,927
Then what are you going to complain about?

183
00:10:54,027 --> 00:10:54,767
Come on, Gurren.

184
00:10:54,827 --> 00:10:56,467
I never said I had any complaints.

185
00:10:56,467 --> 00:11:00,707
Many of our comrades were killed.

186
00:11:01,427 --> 00:11:03,147
You don't always handle that well.

187
00:11:03,687 --> 00:11:05,407
I was just worried about you, that's all.

188
00:11:06,947 --> 00:11:08,427
This was a dangerous mission.

189
00:11:08,807 --> 00:11:10,607
We were bound to lose some good soldiers.

190
00:11:11,107 --> 00:11:13,087
But you're still going to beat yourself up about it.

191
00:11:13,127 --> 00:11:14,227
That's part of your charm.

192
00:11:14,227 --> 00:11:29,907
They're going to be fine.

193
00:11:31,507 --> 00:11:33,247
Even those new troops are elites.

194
00:11:33,867 --> 00:11:35,307
You don't need to worry about them.

195
00:11:35,967 --> 00:11:37,207
You know, you're right.

196
00:11:37,627 --> 00:11:39,087
I should believe in them.

197
00:11:39,927 --> 00:11:41,087
I've got movement here.

198
00:11:44,227 --> 00:11:50,007
You made it.

199
00:11:50,187 --> 00:11:51,347
I was afraid you were dead.

200
00:11:51,947 --> 00:11:53,627
We ran into a lot of trouble.

201
00:11:54,067 --> 00:11:56,227
But we still managed to kill our assigned target.

202
00:11:57,007 --> 00:11:57,907
That's great.

203
00:11:58,567 --> 00:12:00,147
I'm so glad to see you.

204
00:12:06,707 --> 00:12:07,687
Get out of here!

205
00:12:07,947 --> 00:12:09,407
Meet the lieutenant colonel at the airport.

206
00:12:09,407 --> 00:12:11,187
I can take care of this myself.

207
00:12:14,227 --> 00:12:39,227
Damn you!

208
00:12:39,227 --> 00:12:56,527
Hello, human.

209
00:12:57,247 --> 00:12:59,247
You're going to answer some questions for me.

210
00:12:59,247 --> 00:13:12,667
Everyone!

211
00:13:13,167 --> 00:13:14,827
This is the code 284!

212
00:13:14,827 --> 00:13:27,427
Everyone!

213
00:13:27,887 --> 00:13:29,487
This is the code 284!

214
00:13:29,487 --> 00:13:53,367
What's going on?

215
00:13:53,367 --> 00:13:54,927
I was barely choking him.

216
00:13:55,347 --> 00:13:56,947
The humans have poisoned themselves.

217
00:13:57,347 --> 00:13:58,807
Now we can't torture them.

218
00:13:58,807 --> 00:14:02,107
So you've got some kind of suicide pill in your mouth.

219
00:14:02,387 --> 00:14:03,987
But I can't let you die yet.

220
00:14:04,367 --> 00:14:06,227
I have a question I need to ask you.

221
00:14:08,727 --> 00:14:10,347
Torture me all you want, bastard!

222
00:14:10,707 --> 00:14:11,847
I'm not going to tell you a damn-

223
00:14:11,847 --> 00:14:12,427
Keep quiet!

224
00:14:13,987 --> 00:14:15,047
Pretend you're dead too.

225
00:14:15,947 --> 00:14:18,587
You don't want the other vampires to find out you're alive.

226
00:14:18,587 --> 00:14:23,367
I'll let you go if you answer my questions truthfully.

227
00:14:23,767 --> 00:14:24,107
Got it?

228
00:14:28,887 --> 00:14:31,727
Do you know a human named Yuichiro Hyakuya?

229
00:14:38,387 --> 00:14:40,787
I can see from the look in your eyes that you do.

230
00:14:41,567 --> 00:14:43,367
Tell me where he is if you want to live.

231
00:14:43,367 --> 00:14:46,087
Kill me!

232
00:14:46,667 --> 00:14:48,087
I won't tell out my comrade to-

233
00:14:48,087 --> 00:14:48,707
Shut up!

234
00:14:49,047 --> 00:14:51,227
You don't get to call yourself Yu's comrade!

235
00:14:54,047 --> 00:14:54,807
Hold on.

236
00:14:56,087 --> 00:14:57,027
Who are you?

237
00:14:58,007 --> 00:14:58,407
Really?

238
00:14:58,407 --> 00:15:00,447
Hey, Mika.

239
00:15:00,787 --> 00:15:02,327
What are you doing over there?

240
00:15:03,827 --> 00:15:05,247
Just checking on this human.

241
00:15:05,547 --> 00:15:06,487
But she's dead too.

242
00:15:08,287 --> 00:15:10,007
Why'd they go and kill themselves?

243
00:15:10,327 --> 00:15:11,067
Are they stupid?

244
00:15:12,067 --> 00:15:12,387
Hey!

245
00:15:12,627 --> 00:15:13,227
Over here!

246
00:15:13,507 --> 00:15:13,707
Hmm?

247
00:15:14,887 --> 00:15:15,807
Find something.

248
00:15:16,447 --> 00:15:17,307
Look at this.

249
00:15:18,007 --> 00:15:19,847
Several vampires were killed here.

250
00:15:19,847 --> 00:15:24,887
From the look of these clothes, I'd say Lukal Wesker's dead.

251
00:15:25,427 --> 00:15:25,987
No way.

252
00:15:26,267 --> 00:15:29,507
An entire army of humans wouldn't be able to kill a noble like him.

253
00:15:30,187 --> 00:15:30,807
Lord Lachis!

254
00:15:31,047 --> 00:15:31,447
Lord Rene!

255
00:15:31,907 --> 00:15:32,127
Hmm?

256
00:15:32,827 --> 00:15:34,967
The vampires underground have been wiped out!

257
00:15:35,687 --> 00:15:37,147
What about Lord Mel Stefano?

258
00:15:37,827 --> 00:15:40,347
We searched the tunnels, but we can't find him anywhere.

259
00:15:40,947 --> 00:15:41,427
Seriously?

260
00:15:42,427 --> 00:15:45,267
Something strange is going on here, and I don't like it.

261
00:15:46,067 --> 00:15:46,587
Me neither.

262
00:15:47,047 --> 00:15:47,727
Let's get moving.

263
00:15:47,727 --> 00:15:49,627
Lord Crowley should be at City Hall.

264
00:15:49,767 --> 00:15:50,747
He'll know what happened here.

265
00:15:53,027 --> 00:15:54,127
Stop right there!

266
00:15:56,827 --> 00:15:59,047
Make one move, and I'll slit your friend's throat!

267
00:16:00,007 --> 00:16:03,647
Mika, I know you're kind of slow sometimes, but how did you miss that she was alive?

268
00:16:04,147 --> 00:16:04,807
Capture her.

269
00:16:05,047 --> 00:16:05,967
She'll prove useful.

270
00:16:06,307 --> 00:16:07,747
I told you not to move!

271
00:16:07,947 --> 00:16:09,687
Do you want this bloodsucker to die?

272
00:16:09,947 --> 00:16:11,347
You can do whatever you want.

273
00:16:11,547 --> 00:16:13,127
If he dies, it's his own fault.

274
00:16:13,667 --> 00:16:14,367
Hold on.

275
00:16:14,647 --> 00:16:16,027
I'll take care of this mess.

276
00:16:16,027 --> 00:16:16,947
Shut your mouth!

277
00:16:19,627 --> 00:16:24,247
All right.

278
00:16:24,427 --> 00:16:25,467
So, Hiyakuya.

279
00:16:26,227 --> 00:16:28,107
He left for City Hall not long ago.

280
00:16:32,647 --> 00:16:35,627
If you and your friends go there too, everyone will be killed.

281
00:16:35,627 --> 00:16:38,667
Why are you telling me this now?

282
00:16:41,147 --> 00:16:42,587
Because you called him you.

283
00:16:43,067 --> 00:16:45,107
I'm hoping that means you're a friend of his.

284
00:16:45,407 --> 00:16:47,767
That's all the intelligence I have about Hiyakuya.

285
00:16:48,727 --> 00:16:50,267
Do you understand what that means?

286
00:16:57,227 --> 00:16:57,727
Die!

287
00:16:57,727 --> 00:17:10,047
Not bad.

288
00:17:11,427 --> 00:17:17,067
You had the rest of your men commit suicide, but here you are acting like a desperate fool trying to save your own life.

289
00:17:17,067 --> 00:17:20,007
You want to live that badly?

290
00:17:20,707 --> 00:17:21,807
I don't want to die!

291
00:17:22,147 --> 00:17:23,087
Please don't kill me!

292
00:17:26,087 --> 00:17:28,067
Then tell me where your comrades are.

293
00:17:28,327 --> 00:17:31,107
Your squad is obviously too weak to be behind these attacks.

294
00:17:32,107 --> 00:17:35,987
If I tell you, then you're not going to kill me, okay?

295
00:17:37,067 --> 00:17:37,507
Right.

296
00:17:37,507 --> 00:17:47,227
The Imperial Army's strongest soldiers are at this moment heading to the Botanical Garden in Higashiyama Park.

297
00:17:48,027 --> 00:17:50,347
Their mission is to execute Zane Lindau.

298
00:17:53,947 --> 00:17:55,087
Do you know him?

299
00:17:55,547 --> 00:17:57,487
How do you not know who he is?

300
00:17:57,887 --> 00:17:59,747
Lindau is the 17th progenitor.

301
00:17:59,747 --> 00:18:03,707
So they know the name of a noble and where he's located.

302
00:18:04,787 --> 00:18:07,107
This whole setup gives me a bad feeling.

303
00:18:07,367 --> 00:18:08,167
What should we do?

304
00:18:08,627 --> 00:18:10,347
We have to go and warn Lord Lindau.

305
00:18:10,587 --> 00:18:12,047
Otherwise, we'll end up in big trouble.

306
00:18:12,467 --> 00:18:12,867
Let's go.

307
00:18:14,847 --> 00:18:16,227
That's super far away.

308
00:18:16,307 --> 00:18:17,647
This is going to be such a pain.

309
00:18:22,687 --> 00:18:23,167
Wait.

310
00:18:25,207 --> 00:18:26,227
Please kill me.

311
00:18:26,847 --> 00:18:27,247
Quickly.

312
00:18:29,747 --> 00:18:32,667
I've no reason to live.

313
00:18:33,187 --> 00:18:34,307
There's nothing left.

314
00:18:35,127 --> 00:18:36,847
I'm not getting my hands dirty.

315
00:18:37,147 --> 00:18:38,967
If you want to die, kill yourself.

316
00:18:39,347 --> 00:18:40,007
I can't.

317
00:18:40,447 --> 00:18:41,307
I kill myself.

318
00:18:41,727 --> 00:18:43,927
And they'll start to doubt the information I gave them.

319
00:18:44,447 --> 00:18:46,547
But if you were to kill me, they wouldn't bat an eye.

320
00:18:51,987 --> 00:18:52,947
Hey, Mika.

321
00:18:53,387 --> 00:18:55,347
If you don't hurry up, we'll leave you behind.

322
00:18:59,747 --> 00:19:02,007
And bring that pathetic human.

323
00:19:02,387 --> 00:19:02,827
Come on.

324
00:19:05,647 --> 00:19:07,867
I think she told us everything she knows.

325
00:19:08,387 --> 00:19:09,127
Not yet.

326
00:19:09,427 --> 00:19:11,307
We can still get more information out of...

327
00:19:11,307 --> 00:19:12,447
Look out!

328
00:19:15,087 --> 00:19:16,087
You bastards!

329
00:19:16,427 --> 00:19:17,347
I know your game.

330
00:19:17,427 --> 00:19:19,147
You're eventually going to kill me anyway.

331
00:19:19,147 --> 00:19:37,467
I'll be there, hold on.

332
00:19:37,527 --> 00:19:40,287
Death trail through somehow.

333
00:19:41,287 --> 00:19:44,047
Somewhere I am now.

334
00:19:44,047 --> 00:19:46,447
Oh, man.

335
00:19:46,507 --> 00:19:48,027
You killed her before we got to play.

336
00:19:48,527 --> 00:19:50,887
Who cares about what the livestock has to say?

337
00:19:51,527 --> 00:19:53,147
Well, you've got a point there.

338
00:19:54,107 --> 00:19:57,167
The blind loyalty these humans have is a little frightening.

339
00:19:57,527 --> 00:20:03,167
The Japanese Imperial Demon Army may prove to be more of a problem than we expected.

340
00:20:03,167 --> 00:20:06,727
True, these humans are nothing alone.

341
00:20:07,047 --> 00:20:09,127
But when they gang up, they're kind of dangerous.

342
00:20:09,747 --> 00:20:11,387
Let's head to the Botanical Garden.

343
00:20:12,087 --> 00:20:14,967
We can't allow the 17th Progenitor to be killed as well.

344
00:20:15,687 --> 00:20:17,267
I'm gonna take a different route.

345
00:20:19,307 --> 00:20:23,047
This human may have been scared for her life, but we can take her word alone.

346
00:20:24,187 --> 00:20:28,307
Let me borrow five soldiers and I'll go see what's happening at City Hall, just in case.

347
00:20:29,487 --> 00:20:30,687
That's not a bad idea.

348
00:20:31,347 --> 00:20:32,587
We'll regroup when you're done.

349
00:20:32,587 --> 00:20:51,387
That story protected you.

350
00:20:51,987 --> 00:20:53,467
Maybe you were his comrade.

351
00:20:54,467 --> 00:20:54,947
No.

352
00:20:55,587 --> 00:20:57,987
You probably just used him like all the others do.

353
00:20:57,987 --> 00:21:09,767
Okay, follow me.

354
00:21:10,047 --> 00:21:11,767
Let's see what's going on at City Hall.

355
00:21:16,547 --> 00:21:18,767
I'm coming, old friend.

356
00:21:18,767 --> 00:21:27,007
Is there something wrong?

357
00:21:27,367 --> 00:21:28,527
Uh, no.

358
00:21:29,147 --> 00:21:30,727
It's just getting really cloudy.

359
00:21:31,367 --> 00:21:33,387
It's the perfect weather to launch an attack.

360
00:21:34,727 --> 00:21:35,087
Yeah.

361
00:21:35,407 --> 00:21:36,487
Let's get on with it.

362
00:21:36,487 --> 00:21:37,487
I'm coming.

363
00:21:38,147 --> 00:21:38,187
I'm coming.

364
00:21:38,227 --> 00:21:38,607
I'm coming.

365
00:21:54,447 --> 00:21:55,087
I'm coming.

366
00:21:55,087 --> 00:21:56,547
I'm coming.

367
00:23:24,945 --> 00:23:35,105
Next time on Seraph of the End, Shinya and Gurin.

